# Testing strategy

Full guide: [backend/TESTING.md](../../TESTING.md). Harness notes: [ARCHITECTURE — testing](../../ARCHITECTURE.md#testing-strategy).

## Absolute rules

1. **Never write unit tests.** Do not add new tests that call production code without HTTP. Features go through [BaseApiTest](../../src/test/kotlin/com/mhaefele/gridiron/integration/support/BaseApiTest.kt) + [GridironApiClient](../../src/test/kotlin/com/mhaefele/gridiron/integration/support/GridironApiClient.kt). Existing domain tests may stay; do not extend them instead of an API test.
2. **API test mandatory** for anything reachable over HTTP. Seed with `seedMatch` / `match { }` + `api.play`, not bean crank.
3. **No `@Autowired` / bean-direct orchestrator tests** without an explicit agreed exception in chat first (`TurnEngine`, `PlayerActionExecutor`, `RegularPlayerActionResolver`, `MatchGame`, …).
4. **Never hand-wire Spring beans** in tests (`Foo(Bar(), Baz())` for `@Component` types).
5. **Spring boots once** — one `@SpringBootTest` on [BaseApiTest](../../src/test/kotlin/com/mhaefele/gridiron/integration/support/BaseApiTest.kt); no `@MockBean` / `@DirtiesContext` per test; reconfigure the same boundary double (`ScriptedDiceRoller`).
6. **No mock-heavy suites** — assert HTTP/persisted outcomes, not `verify(mock)`.

